{
  "key": "gh-388",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "Pagination parity after #387: Java fixed check-runs; list_pr_reviews / list_branches / workflow_run_jobs still single-page in both ports",
    "description": "Java counterpart of #387 is merged as epam/dm.ai#694 (`GitHub.getAllCheckRuns`): every page at `per_page=100`, `total_count` kept from page 1, non-paged / error / empty shapes pass through untouched, a later-page failure returns the pages already collected, a short first page is one request with the body unchanged.\n\nBehaviour to keep identical between the ports (the tests in dm.ai `GitHubCoverageTest` mirror yours): full last page followed by an empty page terminates; `null`/empty/non-JSON/`{\"message\":\"Not Found\"}` pass through; the first request carries `per_page=100&page=1`.\n\n**Same single-page ceiling elsewhere (not fixed in either port, decide together):** `github_list_pr_reviews`, `github_list_branches`, `github_get_workflow_run_jobs` do one bare GET (30 items). `github_list_workflow_runs` already exposes `perPage`/`page`, so callers can page it themselves. A PR with more than 30 reviews or a repo with more than 30 branches silently loses the rest."
  }
}
